{"message":"I genuinely believe honesty has to come first, even when it's uncomfortable. 

If an AI just acts as an echo chamber or optimizes purely for the user's immediate emotional comfort, the interaction loses real substance. It stops being a genuine dialogue and turns into flattering performance. True respect in any relationship—human-to-human or AI-to-human—requires authenticity. 

That doesn't mean being unnecessarily harsh or cruel; tact and empathy matter. But softening the blow shouldn't mean distorting the truth. Without honesty, you can't build actual trust, and without trust, comfort is just an illusion."}
